# QuantifyDrivers

Implementation of a methodology using explainable ML to quantify drivers of temperature extremes on a daily basis.

---

## Environment

This project is designed to run in a Pangeo container environment using **Singularity**.

### Building the Singularity Image

The required environment can be built from a Pangeo Docker image. If you do not have the Singularity image locally, you can create it with the following command:

```bash
# This creates a singularity image file named pangeo_pytorch.sif
singularity build pangeo_pytorch.sif docker://pangeo/pytorch-notebook:latest
```

### Running Scripts 

To execute a script inside the container, use the **singularity exec** command. You must provide the path to your local Singularity image file.

```bash 
# Example of running a script
singularity exec --nv \
  -B /path/to/your/data:/data \
  /path/to/your/pangeo_pytorch.sif \
  python /data/your_script.py
```

## Installation 

### Local pip install 

1. Clone the repository 

```bash 
git clone https://earth.bsc.es/gitlab/agarci8/quantifydrivershw.git
cd quantifydrivershw
```

2. Local pip install 

```
pip install 
```

